{
  "about": "S-notifications - the frames and the undrawn states of Értesítések (/notifications, PLAN 4.1 rule 7). Replay only: M (user@) for every list state, N (demo.nagy.balazs@) for the empty frame. Nothing is written live: the mark-read POST the page fires on opening is the declared default stub (204) of pulse-frames.json, or a per-state stub below. The recorded M inbox holds eight rows of kinds no server code writes (streak, coins, plan, nutrition ...); every list state therefore replaces the list with rows of the two kinds the server really writes (backend/src/db/worker.js:941 chat.message - title = the sender e-mail local part, no body, link /chat/<id>; :3880 profile.equipment_changed - the fixed title and body, link /settings), with the frame's ages against the freeze instant 2026-10-15T15:08:35Z. A chat row carries no body key: the server writes no body (null) and the recordings only ever hold a string there, so pulse-fixture-check refuses null; the page reads a missing body exactly as null (no sub line). Such states are matched-fixture at best.",
